# GF180MCU: GlobalFoundries 0.18 um 3.3 V / 5 V / 6 V MCU process, open PDK.
#
# Stack this deck describes: 1P6M, 9 kA MetalTop, MIM option B (MiM between
# Metal5 and MetalTop), stack option 16 of the design manual's metal-option
# table. For another stack, change the metal loops and the MIMTM block.
#
# Sources, each pinned to the commit the numbers were read from:
#   [DRM] GF180MCU design manual, google/gf180mcu-pdk @ df0f549be9c6b9290bd663ab862ea886680f9e30
#         https://github.com/google/gf180mcu-pdk/tree/main/docs/physical_verification/design_manual/tables_clear
#         (rendered at https://gf180mcu-pdk.readthedocs.io): layer map (06_Drawn_layer),
#         rule tables 10..28, 55, 56, device list (69), electromigration (54).
#   [KL]  GF180MCU KLayout DRC and LVS decks,
#         google/globalfoundries-pdk-libs-gf180mcu_fd_pr @ b239189ef05aa6c83d241799163695b70f78d0d1
#         https://github.com/google/globalfoundries-pdk-libs-gf180mcu_fd_pr/tree/main/rules/klayout
#         (gf180mcu.drc, gf180mcu_antenna.drc, gf180mcu_density.drc, gf180mcu.lvs): rule ids,
#         the 3.3 V / 5 V split, derived layers and device recognition.
#   [PV]  GF180MCU KLayout DRC deck and its unit test structures,
#         fossi-foundation/globalfoundries-pdk-libs-gf180mcu_fd_pv @ b390a163ab86205006038a4a7eff73b17d54b814
#         klayout/drc (rule_decks/*.rb, generic_layers.rb; testing/unit/*.gds, whose pass and
#         fail boxes on 2/222 and 3/222 say what each rule must flag; ledger docs/xcheck/gf180mcu.tsv).
#   [SPEC] GF180MCU analog specs, google/gf180mcu-pdk @ df0f549, docs/analog/layout/inter_specs
#         tables 3 (conductor thickness), 4 (dielectric k), 5 (sheet resistance);
#         docs/analog/model_parameters/LV tables 03, 06, 07 (model names).
#   [MAG] open_pdks Magic tech file gf180mcu.tech,
#         RTimothyEdwards/open_pdks @ 931e0cf509908b1fa8d222bbd8e24e4a36526157 (file last changed 2026-06-15)
#         https://github.com/RTimothyEdwards/open_pdks/blob/master/gf180mcu/magic/gf180mcu.tech
#         (layer heights, contact resistance, substrate area and fringe caps, typical corner).
#
# Each intra-layer spacing rule is KLayout `space` in [PV], which also
# measures a notch inside one polygon, and the fd_pv unit structures
# (klayout/drc/testing/unit) draw notches as fails; GPurify's `space` pairs
# distinct figures, so each such rule has a `<id>.notch` row (not PRES.2 and
# LRES.2, which [PV] checks with `isolated`, nor the cut layers).
#
# Rule ids are the manual's. Where the manual gives different 3.3 V and 5 V/6 V
# limits the id carries the KLayout deck's `_3.3V` / `_5V` suffix; the 3.3 V
# limit is applied to every shape (it is the smaller one) and the 5 V limit to
# the shapes touching DUALGATE. Where both are equal the id has no suffix.

grid 5nm                                    # [DRM] GRID: integer multiple of 0.005 um

# Drawn layers [DRM 06_Drawn_layer]
layer dnwell = gds(12, 0)
layer nwell = gds(21, 0)
layer lvpwell = gds(204, 0)
layer comp = gds(22, 0)
layer dualgate = gds(55, 0)
layer poly2 = gds(30, 0)
layer nplus = gds(32, 0)
layer pplus = gds(31, 0)
layer sab = gds(49, 0)
layer esd = gds(24, 0)
layer contact = gds(33, 0)
layer metal1 = gds(34, 0)
layer via1 = gds(35, 0)
layer metal2 = gds(36, 0)
layer via2 = gds(38, 0)
layer metal3 = gds(42, 0)
layer via3 = gds(40, 0)
layer metal4 = gds(46, 0)
layer via4 = gds(41, 0)
layer metal5 = gds(81, 0)
layer via5 = gds(82, 0)
layer metaltop = gds(53, 0)
layer pad = gds(37, 0)
layer resistor = gds(62, 0)
layer fusetop = gds(75, 0)
layer nat = gds(5, 0)
layer mvsd = gds(210, 0)
layer mvpsd = gds(11, 39)
layer poly2_dummy = gds(30, 4)
layer metal1_dummy = gds(34, 4)
layer metal2_dummy = gds(36, 4)
layer metal3_dummy = gds(42, 4)
layer metal4_dummy = gds(46, 4)
layer metal5_dummy = gds(81, 4)
layer metaltop_dummy = gds(53, 4)

# Text layers [DRM 06_Drawn_layer, "LABEL drawn at ..."]
layer comp_label = gds(22, 10)
layer poly2_label = gds(30, 10)
layer metal1_label = gds(34, 10)
layer metal2_label = gds(36, 10)
layer metal3_label = gds(42, 10)
layer metal4_label = gds(46, 10)
layer metal5_label = gds(81, 10)
layer metaltop_label = gds(53, 10)

# Marking layers [DRM 06_Drawn_layer]
layer res_mk = gds(110, 5)
layer v5_xtor = gds(112, 1)
layer cap_mk = gds(117, 5)
layer mos_cap_mk = gds(166, 5)
layer drc_bjt = gds(127, 5)
layer esd_mk = gds(24, 5)
layer ldmos_xtor = gds(226, 0)
layer plfuse = gds(125, 5)
layer otp_mk = gds(173, 5)
layer metal1_res = gds(110, 11)
layer metal2_res = gds(110, 12)
layer metal3_res = gds(110, 13)
layer metal6_res = gds(110, 16)

# Derived layers, as the KLayout decks define them [KL]
layer ncomp = comp and nplus
layer pcomp = comp and pplus
layer gate = poly2 and comp
layer ngate = gate and nplus
layer pgate = gate and pplus
layer gate_hv = gate and dualgate
layer comp_hv = comp.interacting(dualgate)
layer poly2_hv = poly2.interacting(dualgate).outside(plfuse)
layer nwell_hv = nwell.interacting(dualgate)
layer lvpwell_hv = lvpwell.interacting(dualgate)
layer dnwell_hv = dnwell.interacting(dualgate)
layer nwell_out_dn = nwell.outside(dnwell)
layer nwell_in_dn = nwell.interacting(dnwell)
layer lvpwell_in_dn = lvpwell.inside(dnwell)
# LVPWELL touching DNWELL, which LPW.3 holds; LVPWELL wholly outside is LPW.11's [PV generic_layers.rb lvpwell_dn].
layer lvpwell_dn = lvpwell.interacting(dnwell)
layer lvpwell_out_dn = lvpwell.outside(dnwell)
# An Nwell resistor is Nwell under a RES_MK that reaches past the well [PV
# nwell.rb nw_res_mk]; its taps' COMP stays in it, so NW.1b measures the
# resistor's full width, not the strips beside the taps.
layer nw_res_mk = res_mk.interacting(nwell) not res_mk.inside(nwell)
layer nwell_res = nwell_out_dn and nw_res_mk
layer comp_moscap = comp and mos_cap_mk
layer comp_in_moscap = comp.inside(mos_cap_mk)
layer comp_nocap = comp not comp_in_moscap
layer comp_bjt = comp.inside(drc_bjt)

# Well taps (LVS ntap / ptap), and the rest of COMP as source/drain [KL gf180mcu.lvs]
layer ntap = ncomp.inside(nwell) not res_mk
layer ptap = pcomp.outside(nwell).outside(dnwell) not res_mk
layer sd = comp not poly2 not res_mk not ntap not ptap
layer poly2_con = poly2 not res_mk not plfuse
layer metal1_con = metal1 not metal1_res
layer metal2_con = metal2 not metal2_res
layer metal3_con = metal3 not metal3_res
layer metaltop_con = metaltop not metal6_res
# A Via5 landing on the MIM top plate joins FuseTop to MetalTop, not Metal5.
layer via5_nomim = via5 not fusetop

# COMP classes for the DF rules [KL]
layer ntap_dn = ncomp.outside(lvpwell).inside(dnwell)
layer ntap_dn_hv = ntap_dn.interacting(dualgate)
layer ncomp_notgate = ncomp.not_interacting(gate)
layer ncomp_dn = ncomp_notgate.interacting(dnwell)
layer ncomp_dn_hv = ncomp_dn.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_out_dn = pcomp.outside(dnwell)
layer pcomp_nw = pcomp_out_dn.interacting(nwell)
layer pcomp_nw_hv = pcomp_nw.interacting(dualgate)
layer ncomp_out_dn = ncomp.outside(dnwell)
layer ncomp_nw = ncomp_out_dn.interacting(nwell)
layer ncomp_nw_hv = ncomp_nw.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_dn = pcomp.interacting(dnwell)
layer pcomp_dn_hv = pcomp_dn.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_out_nw = pcomp.outside(nwell)
layer pcomp_lvp = pcomp_out_nw.interacting(lvpwell_in_dn)
layer pcomp_lvp_hv = pcomp_lvp.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_in_dn = pcomp.inside(dnwell)
layer pcomp_dn_nolvp = pcomp_in_dn.outside(lvpwell)
layer pcomp_dn_nolvp_hv = pcomp_dn_nolvp.interacting(dualgate)
layer ncomp_in_dn = ncomp.inside(dnwell)
layer ncomp_lvp = ncomp_in_dn.interacting(lvpwell)
layer ncomp_lvp_hv = ncomp_lvp.interacting(dualgate)
layer ncomp_psub = ncomp.outside(nwell).outside(dnwell)
layer ncomp_psub_hv = ncomp_psub.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_psub = pcomp.outside(nwell).outside(dnwell)
layer pcomp_psub_hv = pcomp_psub.interacting(dualgate)
layer pcomp_in_nw = pcomp.inside(nwell)
layer pcomp_in_nw_hv = pcomp_in_nw.interacting(dualgate)
layer ncomp_out_nw = ncomp.outside(nwell)
layer ncomp_out_nw_hv = ncomp_out_nw.interacting(dualgate)
layer comp_out_dv = comp.outside(dualgate)
layer comp_dv = comp_hv not ptap
# Poly2 sharing no area with COMP; one touching COMP only at a corner is
# field poly 0 um from it [DRM PL.5a; PV poly2.rb].
layer poly2_field = poly2.outside(comp)
layer comp_hv_noext = comp_hv.outside(mvsd).outside(mvpsd)

# Implant, SAB and ESD classes [KL]
layer poly_sab = poly2 and sab
# Unrelated unsalicided Poly2 shares no area with the implant; touching it at
# a corner is 0 um from it [PV nplus.rb NP.7, pplus.rb PP.7].
layer poly_sab_nonp = poly_sab.outside(nplus)
layer poly_sab_nopp = poly_sab.outside(pplus)
layer poly_sab_np = poly_sab.interacting(nplus)
layer poly_sab_pp = poly_sab.not_interacting(resistor).interacting(pplus)
layer comp_sab = comp and sab
layer comp_sab_np = comp_sab.interacting(nplus)
layer comp_sab_pp = comp_sab.interacting(pplus)
# The OTP section states its own SAB rules (O.SB.*): SB.2-SB.5b, SB.9 and
# SB.11-SB.13 hold SAB outside OTP_MK [PV sab.rb sab_out_otp].
layer sab_main = sab.outside(otp_mk)
layer sab_field = sab_main.outside(comp)
layer comp_nosab = comp.outside(sab)
layer poly2_on_field = poly2 not comp
layer sab_off_pf = sab_main.outside(poly2_on_field)
layer pf_nosab = poly2_on_field.outside(sab)
layer sab_off_gate = sab_main.outside(gate)
layer gate_nosab = gate.outside(sab)
layer sab_noesd = sab_main.outside(esd_mk)
layer poly2_noesd = poly2.outside(esd_mk)
layer ncomp_out_esd = ncomp.outside(esd)
layer implant = nplus or pplus
layer implant_out_esd = implant.outside(esd)

# Contact classes [KL]
layer contact_poly = contact.interacting(poly2)
layer contact_comp = contact.interacting(comp)

# MIM option B: FuseTop over the Metal5 bottom plate [KL MIMTM]
layer metal5_mim = metal5.interacting(fusetop)
layer mimtm_virtual = fusetop.sized(1060nm) and metal5_mim
layer metal5_nomim = metal5.not_interacting(fusetop)
layer via5_on_mim = via5.interacting(mimtm_virtual)
layer via5_top = via5.interacting(fusetop)
layer via5_in_top = via5.inside(fusetop)

# Native Vt [KL NAT]
layer ncomp_nat = ncomp.outside(nwell).interacting(nat)
layer comp_out_nat = comp.outside(nat)
layer nat_hv = nat.interacting(dualgate)

# Poly2 resistors [KL PRES / LRES / HRES]
layer pres_poly = (poly2 and pplus).interacting(sab).interacting(res_mk).not_interacting(resistor)
layer lres_poly = (poly2 and nplus).interacting(sab).interacting(res_mk)
layer hres_poly = poly2.interacting(pplus).interacting(sab).interacting(res_mk).interacting(resistor)
layer poly2_nosab = poly2.not_interacting(sab)
layer contact_pres = contact.inside(pres_poly)
layer contact_lres = contact.inside(lres_poly)
layer contact_hres = contact.inside(hres_poly)
layer resistor_h = resistor.interacting(hres_poly)

# Density: the manual counts dummy fill toward coverage [DRM Mn.4, MT.3, PL.8]
layer poly2_fill = poly2 or poly2_dummy
layer metal1_fill = metal1 or metal1_dummy
layer metal2_fill = metal2 or metal2_dummy
layer metal3_fill = metal3 or metal3_dummy
layer metal4_fill = metal4 or metal4_dummy
layer metal5_fill = metal5 or metal5_dummy
layer metaltop_fill = metaltop or metaltop_dummy

# Device markers, mutually exclusive [KL gf180mcu.lvs; model names DRM 69 / SPEC LV 03, 06, 07]
layer ng = (ngate not sab not esd_mk).not_interacting(mos_cap_mk)
layer pg = (pgate not sab not esd_mk).not_interacting(mos_cap_mk)
layer nfet_03v3_g = ng not dualgate
layer pfet_03v3_g = pg not dualgate
layer nfet_06v0_g = ng and dualgate not nat not ldmos_xtor
layer pfet_06v0_g = pg and dualgate not ldmos_xtor
layer nfet_06v0_nvt_g = ng and dualgate and nat
layer nfet_03v3_dss_g = (ngate and esd_mk not dualgate).interacting(sab)
layer pfet_03v3_dss_g = (pgate and esd_mk not dualgate).interacting(sab)
layer nfet_06v0_dss_g = (ngate and esd_mk and dualgate).interacting(sab)
layer pfet_06v0_dss_g = (pgate and esd_mk and dualgate).interacting(sab)
layer cap_nmos_03v3_b_g = (ngate not dualgate).interacting(mos_cap_mk).inside(nwell)
layer cap_pmos_03v3_b_g = (pgate not dualgate).interacting(mos_cap_mk).outside(nwell)
layer cap_nmos_06v0_b_g = (ngate and dualgate).interacting(mos_cap_mk).inside(nwell)
layer cap_pmos_06v0_b_g = (pgate and dualgate).interacting(mos_cap_mk).outside(nwell)
layer npolyf_u_r = poly2 and nplus and sab and res_mk
layer ppolyf_u_r = (poly2 and pplus and sab and res_mk).not_interacting(resistor)
layer npolyf_s_r = (poly2 and nplus and res_mk).not_interacting(sab)
layer ppolyf_s_r = (poly2 and pplus and res_mk).not_interacting(sab)
layer ppolyf_u_1k_r = poly2 and sab and res_mk and resistor not dualgate
layer ppolyf_u_1k_6p0_r = poly2 and sab and res_mk and resistor and dualgate
layer nplus_u_r = ncomp and sab and res_mk
layer pplus_u_r = pcomp and sab and res_mk
layer nplus_s_r = (ncomp and res_mk).not_interacting(sab)
layer pplus_s_r = (pcomp and res_mk).not_interacting(sab)
layer rm1_r = metal1 and metal1_res
layer rm2_r = metal2 and metal2_res
layer rm3_r = metal3 and metal3_res
layer tm9k_r = metaltop and metal6_res

# --- DNWELL [DRM 11, KL] ---
rule DN.1 width(dnwell) >= 1.7um
rule DN.2a space(dnwell) >= 2.5um
rule DN.2a.notch notch(dnwell) >= 2.5um

# --- LVPWELL [DRM 12, KL] ---
rule LPW.1_3.3V width(lvpwell) >= 600nm
rule LPW.1_5V width(lvpwell_hv) >= 740nm
rule LPW.2b space(lvpwell) >= 860nm
rule LPW.2b.notch notch(lvpwell) >= 860nm
rule LPW.3 enclosure(lvpwell_dn, dnwell) >= 2.5um
rule LPW.11 space(lvpwell_out_dn, dnwell) >= 1.5um

# --- Nwell [DRM 13, KL] ---
rule NW.1a width(nwell) >= 860nm
rule NW.1b width(nwell_res) >= 2um
rule NW.2a_3.3V space(nwell) >= 600nm
rule NW.2a_3.3V.notch notch(nwell) >= 600nm
rule NW.2a_5V space(nwell_hv) >= 740nm
rule NW.2a_5V.notch notch(nwell_hv) >= 740nm
rule NW.3 space(nwell_out_dn, dnwell) >= 3.1um
rule NW.5 enclosure(nwell_in_dn, dnwell) >= 500nm

# --- COMP [DRM 14, KL] ---
rule DF.1a_3.3V width(comp) >= 220nm
rule DF.1a_5V width(comp_hv) >= 300nm
rule DF.1c width(comp_moscap) >= 1um
# DF.2a is channel width W: a gate's edges on Poly2's edges run across the
# channel, so their length is W (its edges on COMP's are L, PL.2). The gate's
# narrowest width would read a 0.11 um L as W [PV comp.rb DF.2a: COMP not
# Poly2 edges on the gate's].
rule DF.2a_3.3V length(gate.edges() and poly2.edges()) >= 220nm
rule DF.2a_5V length(gate_hv.edges() and poly2.edges()) >= 300nm
rule DF.2b width(comp_nocap) <= 100um
rule DF.3a_3.3V space(comp) >= 280nm
rule DF.3a_3.3V.notch notch(comp) >= 280nm
rule DF.3a_5V space(comp_hv) >= 360nm
rule DF.3a_5V.notch notch(comp_hv) >= 360nm
rule DF.3c_3.3V space(comp_bjt) >= 320nm
rule DF.3c_3.3V.notch notch(comp_bjt) >= 320nm
rule DF.4a_3.3V space(ntap_dn, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 120nm
rule DF.4a_5V space(ntap_dn_hv, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 160nm
rule DF.4b_3.3V enclosure(ncomp_dn, dnwell) >= 620nm
rule DF.4b_5V enclosure(ncomp_dn_hv, dnwell) >= 660nm
rule DF.4c_3.3V enclosure(pcomp_nw, nwell) >= 430nm
rule DF.4c_5V enclosure(pcomp_nw_hv, nwell) >= 600nm
rule DF.4d_3.3V enclosure(ncomp_nw, nwell) >= 120nm
rule DF.4d_5V enclosure(ncomp_nw_hv, nwell) >= 160nm
rule DF.4e_3.3V enclosure(pcomp_dn, dnwell) >= 930nm
rule DF.4e_5V enclosure(pcomp_dn_hv, dnwell) >= 1.1um
rule DF.5_3.3V enclosure(pcomp_lvp, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 120nm
rule DF.5_5V enclosure(pcomp_lvp_hv, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 160nm
rule DF.6_3.3V extension(comp, poly2) >= 240nm
rule DF.6_5V extension(comp_hv_noext, poly2) >= 400nm
rule DF.7_3.3V space(pcomp_dn_nolvp, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 430nm
rule DF.7_5V space(pcomp_dn_nolvp_hv, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 600nm
rule DF.8_3.3V enclosure(ncomp_lvp, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 430nm
rule DF.8_5V enclosure(ncomp_lvp_hv, lvpwell_in_dn) >= 600nm
rule DF.9 area(comp) >= 0.2025um2
# Field area: the empty area a COMP encloses, less any COMP island in it
# [PV comp.rb DF.10 comp.holes.not(comp)]; hole_area counts the island.
rule DF.10 area(comp.holes() not comp) >= 0.26um2
rule DF.13_3.3V tap_distance(pcomp_in_nw, ntap) <= 20um
rule DF.13_5V tap_distance(pcomp_in_nw_hv, ntap) <= 15um
rule DF.14_3.3V tap_distance(ncomp_out_nw, ptap) <= 20um
rule DF.14_5V tap_distance(ncomp_out_nw_hv, ptap) <= 15um
rule DF.16_3.3V space(ncomp_psub, nwell_out_dn) >= 430nm
rule DF.16_5V space(ncomp_psub_hv, nwell_out_dn) >= 600nm
rule DF.17_3.3V space(pcomp_psub, nwell_out_dn) >= 120nm
rule DF.17_5V space(pcomp_psub_hv, nwell_out_dn) >= 160nm
rule DF.18 space(pcomp_psub, dnwell) >= 2.5um
rule DF.19_3.3V space(ncomp_psub, dnwell) >= 3.2um
rule DF.19_5V space(ncomp_psub_hv, dnwell) >= 3.28um

# --- Dualgate [DRM 15, KL] ---
rule DV.1 enclosure(dnwell_hv, dualgate) >= 500nm
rule DV.2 space(dualgate) >= 440nm
rule DV.2.notch notch(dualgate) >= 440nm
rule DV.3 space(dualgate, comp_out_dv) >= 240nm
rule DV.5 width(dualgate) >= 700nm
rule DV.6 enclosure(comp_dv, dualgate) >= 240nm
rule DV.8 enclosure(poly2_hv, dualgate) >= 400nm

# --- Poly2 [DRM 16, KL; PL.8 from gf180mcu_density.drc] ---
rule PL.1_3.3V width(poly2) >= 180nm
rule PL.1_5V width(poly2_hv) >= 200nm
# PL.2 gate length: a gate's edges on COMP's edges run along the channel, so
# their length is L (its edges on poly's edges are W). The 3.3V floor is on
# every gate (the 5V/6V floors are higher, so it never flags one they pass);
# the 5V floors bound 6V too.
rule PL.2_3.3V length(gate.edges() and comp.edges()) >= 280nm
rule PL.2_5V_n length((ngate and dualgate).edges() and comp.edges()) >= 600nm
rule PL.2_5V_p length((pgate and dualgate).edges() and comp.edges()) >= 500nm
rule PL.3a space(poly2) >= 240nm
rule PL.3a.notch notch(poly2) >= 240nm
rule PL.4 extension(poly2, comp) >= 220nm
# PL.5a/5b hold field poly to COMP; this covers poly shapes with no gate at all.
rule PL.5a_3.3V space(poly2_field, comp) >= 100nm
rule PL.5a_5V space(poly2_field, comp_hv) >= 300nm
rule PL.8 global_density(poly2_fill) >= 14%

# --- Nplus / Pplus [DRM 17, 18, KL] ---
rule NP.1 width(nplus) >= 400nm
rule NP.2 space(nplus) >= 400nm
rule NP.2.notch notch(nplus) >= 400nm
rule NP.5a enclosure(ngate, nplus) >= 230nm
rule NP.7 space(nplus, poly_sab_nonp) >= 180nm
rule NP.8a area(nplus) >= 0.35um2
rule NP.8b hole_area(nplus) >= 0.35um2
rule NP.9 enclosure(poly_sab_np, nplus) >= 180nm
rule NP.10 enclosure(comp_sab_np, nplus) >= 180nm
rule PP.1 width(pplus) >= 400nm
rule PP.2 space(pplus) >= 400nm
rule PP.2.notch notch(pplus) >= 400nm
rule PP.5a enclosure(pgate, pplus) >= 230nm
rule PP.7 space(pplus, poly_sab_nopp) >= 180nm
rule PP.8a area(pplus) >= 0.35um2
rule PP.8b hole_area(pplus) >= 0.35um2
rule PP.9 enclosure(poly_sab_pp, pplus) >= 180nm
rule PP.10 enclosure(comp_sab_pp, pplus) >= 180nm

# --- SAB [DRM 19, KL] ---
rule SB.1 width(sab) >= 420nm
rule SB.2 space(sab_main) >= 420nm
rule SB.2.notch notch(sab_main) >= 420nm
rule SB.3 space(sab_field, comp_nosab) >= 220nm
rule SB.4 space(sab_main, contact) >= 150nm
rule SB.5a space(sab_off_pf, pf_nosab) >= 300nm
rule SB.5b space(sab_off_gate, gate_nosab) >= 280nm
rule SB.6 extension(sab, comp) >= 220nm
rule SB.7 extension(comp, sab) >= 220nm
rule SB.9 extension(sab_main, poly2) >= 220nm
rule SB.10 extension(poly2, sab) >= 220nm
rule SB.11 overlap(sab_main, comp) >= 220nm
rule SB.12 overlap(sab_noesd, poly2_noesd) >= 220nm
rule SB.13 area(sab_main) >= 2um2

# --- ESD implant [DRM 20, KL] ---
rule ESD.1 width(esd) >= 600nm
rule ESD.2 space(esd) >= 600nm
rule ESD.2.notch notch(esd) >= 600nm
rule ESD.3a space(esd, ncomp_out_esd) >= 600nm
rule ESD.4b overlap(esd, comp) >= 450nm
rule ESD.5a area(esd) >= 0.49um2
rule ESD.5b hole_area(esd) >= 0.49um2
rule ESD.8 space(esd, implant_out_esd) >= 300nm

# --- Contact [DRM 21, KL] ---
rule CO.1 size(contact) == 220nm x 220nm
rule CO.2a space(contact) >= 250nm
# CO.2b is "4x4 or larger"; a cluster of more than 15 cuts is held to it.
rule CO.2b via_array_space(contact; array: 15) >= 280nm
rule CO.3 enclosure(contact_poly, poly2) >= 70nm
rule CO.4 enclosure(contact_comp, comp) >= 70nm
rule CO.6 enclosure(contact, metal1) >= 5nm
rule CO.7 space(contact_comp, gate) >= 150nm
rule CO.8 space(contact_poly, comp) >= 170nm

# --- Metaln, n = 1..5 [DRM 22, KL; Mn.4 from gf180mcu_density.drc] ---
let metals = [(M1, metal1, metal1_fill, 230nm), (M2, metal2, metal2_fill, 280nm),
              (M3, metal3, metal3_fill, 280nm), (M4, metal4, metal4_fill, 280nm),
              (M5, metal5, metal5_fill, 280nm)]
for (id, m, fill, w) in metals {
    rule {id}.1 width(m) >= w
    rule {id}.2a space(m) >= w
    rule {id}.2a.notch notch(m) >= w
    rule {id}.2b wide_space(m; width: 10um) >= 300nm
    rule {id}.3 area(m) >= 0.1444um2
    rule {id}.4 global_density(fill) >= 30%
}

# --- Vian, n = 1..5 [DRM 23, KL] ---
# Vn.3 lower metal overlap: 0.00 for Metal1 (V1.3a, under must-contain
# below), 0.01 for Metal2..5 (Vn.3b); Vn.4a upper metal overlap: 0.01.
let vias = [(V1, via1, metal1, metal2), (V2, via2, metal2, metal3),
            (V3, via3, metal3, metal4), (V4, via4, metal4, metal5),
            (V5, via5, metal5, metaltop)]
for (id, v, below, above) in vias {
    rule {id}.1 size(v) == 260nm x 260nm
    rule {id}.2a space(v) >= 260nm
    rule {id}.2b via_array_space(v; array: 15) >= 360nm
    rule {id}.4a enclosure(v, above) >= 10nm
}
let vias_up = [(V2, via2, metal2), (V3, via3, metal3), (V4, via4, metal4), (V5, via5, metal5)]
for (id, v, below) in vias_up {
    rule {id}.3b enclosure(v, below) >= 10nm
}

# --- MetalTop, 9 kA [DRM 24; KL METAL_TOP == "9K"] ---
rule MT.1 width(metaltop) >= 440nm
rule MT.2a space(metaltop) >= 460nm
rule MT.2a.notch notch(metaltop) >= 460nm
rule MT.2b wide_space(metaltop; width: 10um) >= 600nm
rule MT.3 global_density(metaltop_fill) >= 30%
rule MT.4 area(metaltop) >= 0.5625um2

# --- MIM option B, between Metal5 and MetalTop [KL MIMTM] ---
rule MIMTM.1 space(metal5_nomim, mimtm_virtual) >= 1.2um
rule MIMTM.2 enclosure(via5_on_mim, metal5) >= 400nm
rule MIMTM.3 enclosure(fusetop, mimtm_virtual) >= 600nm
rule MIMTM.4 enclosure(via5_top, fusetop) >= 400nm
rule MIMTM.5 space(fusetop, via5_nomim) >= 400nm
rule MIMTM.6 space(fusetop) >= 600nm
rule MIMTM.6.notch notch(fusetop) >= 600nm
rule MIMTM.8a area(fusetop) >= 25um2
rule MIMTM.9 space(via5_in_top) >= 500nm

# --- Native Vt NMOS [DRM 36, KL] ---
rule NAT.1 enclosure(ncomp_nat, nat) >= 2um
rule NAT.2 space(nat, comp_out_nat) >= 300nm
rule NAT.3 space(nat, nwell) >= 500nm
rule NAT.7 space(nat) >= 740nm
rule NAT.7.notch notch(nat) >= 740nm

# --- Poly2 resistors [DRM 33, KL] ---
rule PRES.1 width(pres_poly) >= 800nm
rule PRES.2 space(pres_poly) >= 400nm
rule PRES.3 space(pres_poly, comp) >= 600nm
rule PRES.4 space(pres_poly, poly2_nosab) >= 600nm
rule PRES.5 enclosure(pres_poly, pplus) >= 300nm
rule PRES.7 space(contact_pres, sab) >= 220nm
rule LRES.1 width(lres_poly) >= 800nm
rule LRES.2 space(lres_poly) >= 400nm
rule LRES.3 space(lres_poly, comp) >= 600nm
rule LRES.4 space(lres_poly, poly2_nosab) >= 600nm
rule LRES.5 enclosure(lres_poly, nplus) >= 300nm
rule LRES.7 space(contact_lres, sab) >= 220nm
rule HRES.1 space(resistor_h) >= 400nm
rule HRES.1.notch notch(resistor_h) >= 400nm
rule HRES.2 width(hres_poly) >= 1um
rule HRES.3 space(hres_poly) >= 400nm
rule HRES.3.notch notch(hres_poly) >= 400nm
rule HRES.4 enclosure(hres_poly, resistor) >= 400nm
rule HRES.5 space(resistor_h, poly2_nosab) >= 300nm
rule HRES.6 space(resistor_h, comp) >= 300nm
rule HRES.7 enclosure(contact_hres, pplus) >= 200nm
rule HRES.8 space(contact_hres, sab) >= 220nm

# --- Geometry [DRM 10] ---
rule OFFGRID off_grid(; pitch: 5nm)
rule ACUTE angle(; allowed: [0deg, 45deg, 90deg, 135deg])

# --- Antenna [DRM 27, 28: ratio limits; perimeter-area thickness t per layer, 9 kA MetalTop] ---
# ANT.1-ANT.15 are ratios to the "related gate oxide area", so each rule is one
# row per oxide, the thick (DUALGATE) one suffixed .DG. ANT.16: a failing metal
# or via ratio is checked again with "gate area = (gate area + MF * (COMP area
# directly connection that node))", MF 2 for a thin gate and 15 for a thick
# one, the COMP being any diode, drain or source on the node.
layer gate_thin = gate not dualgate
layer ant_comp = comp not poly2
rule ANT.1 antenna(gate_thin, poly2_con; max_ratio: 200, sidewall: 200nm, diode: none)
rule ANT.1.DG antenna(gate_hv, poly2_con; max_ratio: 200, sidewall: 200nm, diode: none)
let ant_metals = [(ANT.2, ANT.2.DG, metal1_con), (ANT.3, ANT.3.DG, metal2_con),
                  (ANT.4, ANT.4.DG, metal3_con), (ANT.5, ANT.5.DG, metal4),
                  (ANT.6, ANT.6.DG, metal5)]
for (id, dg, m) in ant_metals {
    rule {id} antenna_electrical(gate_thin, m; max_ratio: 400, sidewall: 540nm, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 2,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
    rule {dg} antenna_electrical(gate_hv, m; max_ratio: 400, sidewall: 540nm, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 15,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
}
rule ANT.7 antenna_electrical(gate_thin, metaltop_con; max_ratio: 400, sidewall: 990nm, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 2,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
rule ANT.7.DG antenna_electrical(gate_hv, metaltop_con; max_ratio: 400, sidewall: 990nm, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 15,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
rule ANT.8 antenna(gate_thin, contact; max_ratio: 10, sidewall: none, diode: none)
rule ANT.8.DG antenna(gate_hv, contact; max_ratio: 10, sidewall: none, diode: none)
let ant_vias = [(ANT.9, ANT.9.DG, via1), (ANT.10, ANT.10.DG, via2), (ANT.11, ANT.11.DG, via3),
                (ANT.12, ANT.12.DG, via4), (ANT.13, ANT.13.DG, via5_nomim)]
for (id, dg, v) in ant_vias {
    rule {id} antenna_electrical(gate_thin, v; max_ratio: 20, sidewall: none, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 2,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
    rule {dg} antenna_electrical(gate_hv, v; max_ratio: 20, sidewall: none, cut_factor: 1,
        diode: ant_comp, diode_credit: 0, diode_bonus: 0, area_minus_diode: 0, gate_plus_diode: 15,
        diode_reduce: none, diode_max_ratio: none, exempt: none)
}

# --- Electromigration at 85 C, unidirectional (DC) limits [DRM 54, tables 14.3 and 14.4] ---
# A cut row's max_density is not read (a cut carries per-cut current); it
# restates the wire limit because the parameter is required.
rule EM.14.3_Mn em_current_density(metal1_con, metal2_con, metal3_con, metal4, metal5; max_density: 2.09mA/um, max_current_per_cut: 0.58mA, narrow: none)
rule EM.14.3_MT em_current_density(metaltop_con; max_density: 3.77mA/um, max_current_per_cut: 0.58mA, narrow: none)
rule EM.14.4_Vn em_current_density(via1, via2, via3, via4, via5_nomim; max_density: 2.09mA/um, max_current_per_cut: 0.58mA, narrow: none)
rule EM.14.4_CO em_current_density(contact; max_density: 2.09mA/um, max_current_per_cut: 0.43mA, narrow: none)

# --- Electrical ---
# LU.9 / LU.10: Nwell taps go to the most positive supply and substrate taps to
# the lowest, so one net carrying both is a supply short [DRM 55].
rule LU.9_10 supply_short(ntap, ptap)
rule floating_nwell floating_well(nwell, ntap)
rule floating_lvpwell floating_well(lvpwell_in_dn, pcomp_lvp)
rule floating_gate floating_gate(; labels_are_ports: false)
rule tie_high_low warning tie_high_low()
rule multiple_drivers multiple_drivers(; max: 1)
rule ir_drop ir_drop()
rule unconnected_metaltop warning unconnected_pin(metaltop_con)
# Pads reach both rails through the SAB (ESD) MOSFETs [DRM 69 "ESD (SAB MOSFET)"].
rule ESD.clamp_path esd_topological(pad; clamps: ["nfet_03v3_dss", "pfet_03v3_dss", "nfet_06v0_dss", "pfet_06v0_dss"])
# Operating voltages LV = 3.3 V, HV = 5 V or 6 V [DRM 02_Process_Identification].
# These are the nominal supplies; the open manual publishes no absolute maximum.
let lv = ["nfet_03v3", "pfet_03v3", "nfet_03v3_dss", "pfet_03v3_dss"]
let hv = ["nfet_06v0", "pfet_06v0", "nfet_06v0_nvt", "nfet_06v0_dss", "pfet_06v0_dss"]
rule OX.3v3 gate_oxide(; models: lv, max: 3.3V)
rule OX.6v0 gate_oxide(; models: hv, max: 6V)
rule DS.3v3 drain_source(; models: lv, max: 3.3V)
rule DS.6v0 drain_source(; models: hv, max: 6V)

# --- Connectivity [KL gf180mcu.lvs connect statements] ---
connect conductors [sd, ntap, ptap, poly2_con, metal1_con, metal2_con, metal3_con, metal4, metal5, metaltop_con]
connect touch_within_layer
connect via contact [sd, metal1_con]
connect via contact [ntap, metal1_con]
connect via contact [ptap, metal1_con]
connect via contact [poly2_con, metal1_con]
connect via via1 [metal1_con, metal2_con]
connect via via2 [metal2_con, metal3_con]
connect via via3 [metal3_con, metal4]
connect via via4 [metal4, metal5]
connect via via5_nomim [metal5, metaltop_con]
connect label comp_label names sd
connect label poly2_label names poly2_con
connect label metal1_label names metal1_con
connect label metal2_label names metal2_con
connect label metal3_label names metal3_con
connect label metal4_label names metal4
connect label metal5_label names metal5
connect label metaltop_label names metaltop_con

# --- Devices [KL gf180mcu.lvs; model names DRM 69, SPEC LV 03/06/07] ---
device mos nfet_03v3_g model "nfet_03v3" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos pfet_03v3_g model "pfet_03v3" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
# The 5 V devices (V5_XTOR) use the 6 V models [DRM 69].
device mos nfet_06v0_g model "nfet_06v0" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos pfet_06v0_g model "pfet_06v0" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos nfet_06v0_nvt_g model "nfet_06v0_nvt" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos nfet_03v3_dss_g model "nfet_03v3_dss" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos pfet_03v3_dss_g model "pfet_03v3_dss" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos nfet_06v0_dss_g model "nfet_06v0_dss" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device mos pfet_06v0_dss_g model "pfet_06v0_dss" terminals [poly2_con, sd, sd]
device capacitor cap_nmos_03v3_b_g model "cap_nmos_03v3_b" terminals [poly2_con, ntap]
device capacitor cap_pmos_03v3_b_g model "cap_pmos_03v3_b" terminals [poly2_con, ptap]
device capacitor cap_nmos_06v0_b_g model "cap_nmos_06v0_b" terminals [poly2_con, ntap]
device capacitor cap_pmos_06v0_b_g model "cap_pmos_06v0_b" terminals [poly2_con, ptap]
device resistor npolyf_u_r model "npolyf_u" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
device resistor ppolyf_u_r model "ppolyf_u" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
device resistor npolyf_s_r model "npolyf_s" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
device resistor ppolyf_s_r model "ppolyf_s" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
# The high-Rs poly resistor is 1k, 2k or 3k by process option (KLayout LVS
# switch POLY_RES); this deck takes the 1k option.
device resistor ppolyf_u_1k_r model "ppolyf_u_1k" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
device resistor ppolyf_u_1k_6p0_r model "ppolyf_u_1k_6p0" terminals [poly2_con, poly2_con]
device resistor nplus_u_r model "nplus_u" terminals [sd, sd]
device resistor pplus_u_r model "pplus_u" terminals [sd, sd]
device resistor nplus_s_r model "nplus_s" terminals [sd, sd]
device resistor pplus_s_r model "pplus_s" terminals [sd, sd]
device resistor rm1_r model "rm1" terminals [metal1_con, metal1_con]
device resistor rm2_r model "rm2" terminals [metal2_con, metal2_con]
device resistor rm3_r model "rm3" terminals [metal3_con, metal3_con]
device resistor tm9k_r model "tm9k" terminals [metaltop_con, metaltop_con]

# --- Parasitic stack ---
# thickness: [SPEC 3] typical (MetalTop 9 kA 1.0025 um, M1..M5 0.55, Poly 0.2);
#   diffusion and cut thickness and every height: [MAG] `height` lines.
# sheet: metals [SPEC 5] (M1..M5 0.090, TM 9 kA 0.04 ohm/sq); poly, diffusion
#   and cuts [MAG] typical `resist` / `contact` (n+ 6.3, p+ 7.0, poly 7.3,
#   poly contact 8.0, diffusion contact 6.3/5.2, via 4.5 ohm; the larger kept).
# dielectric: [SPEC 4] IMD, ILD and STI are all k = 4.
# area/fringe cap to substrate: [MAG] typical `defaultareacap` / `defaultperimeter`;
#   diffusion caps are left to the device models, as Magic does.
pex sd thickness 300nm height 14.5nm sheet 7ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex ntap thickness 300nm height 14.5nm sheet 6.3ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex ptap thickness 300nm height 14.5nm sheet 7ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex poly2_con thickness 200nm height 320nm sheet 7.3ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 110.67aF/um2 fringe_cap 50.72aF/um
pex contact thickness 915.5nm height 314.5nm sheet 8ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metal1_con thickness 550nm height 1230nm sheet 0.09ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 29.304aF/um2 fringe_cap 39.431aF/um
pex via1 thickness 600nm height 1780nm sheet 4.5ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metal2_con thickness 550nm height 2380nm sheet 0.09ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 15.016aF/um2 fringe_cap 33.298aF/um
pex via2 thickness 600nm height 2930nm sheet 4.5ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metal3_con thickness 550nm height 3530nm sheet 0.09ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 10.094aF/um2 fringe_cap 30.021aF/um
pex via3 thickness 600nm height 4080nm sheet 4.5ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metal4 thickness 550nm height 4680nm sheet 0.09ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 7.602aF/um2 fringe_cap 28.153aF/um
pex via4 thickness 600nm height 5230nm sheet 4.5ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metal5 thickness 550nm height 5830nm sheet 0.09ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 5.798aF/um2 fringe_cap 30.386aF/um
pex via5_nomim thickness 900nm height 6380nm sheet 4.5ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 0aF/um2 fringe_cap 0aF/um
pex metaltop_con thickness 1002.5nm height 7280nm sheet 0.04ohm dielectric 4 area_cap 4.8793aF/um2 fringe_cap 9.595aF/um

# --- Presence rules ---
rule LPW.12 forbidden(lvpwell and nwell)
rule NW.4 forbidden(nwell and lvpwell)
# An Nwell inside RES_MK and over DNWELL [PV nwell.rb NW.6]; nwell_res is outside DNWELL by construction.
rule NW.6 forbidden(nwell.inside(res_mk) and dnwell)
rule DV.7 forbidden(comp_dv not dualgate)
rule PL.9 forbidden((poly2 and dualgate).interacting(poly2 not dualgate))
rule PL.11 forbidden(v5_xtor.not_interacting(dualgate))
rule PL.12 forbidden(comp.interacting(v5_xtor) not v5_xtor)
rule SB.8 forbidden(contact.inside(sab))
rule ESD.3b forbidden(esd and pcomp)
rule ESD.7 forbidden(esd and pcomp)
rule ESD.9 inside(esd, dualgate)
rule CO.10 forbidden(contact and gate)
rule CO.11 forbidden(contact not (comp or poly2))
rule MIMTM.10 forbidden(via4.interacting(metal5_mim))
rule NAT.10 forbidden(nwell.inside(nat))
rule NAT.11 forbidden((ncomp and nat).outside(poly2))
# Poly2 inside NAT, not poly that only touches it [PV nat.rb NAT.12].
rule NAT.12 forbidden((poly2 and nat).not_interacting(comp) or (poly2 and nat and res_mk))
rule V1.3a inside(via1, metal1)
rule DF.11 length(ncomp.edges() and pcomp.edges()) >= 300nm


# --- Butted COMP, end-of-line, gate length and guard-ring rules [DRM 11, 16, 17,
# 18, 20, 21, 23, 33, 35, 36; PV nplus.rb, pplus.rb, contact.rb, via.rb, esd.rb,
# nat.rb, pres.rb, lres.rb, poly2.rb, mim_b.rb, dnwell.rb] ---
# NP.3d/PP.3d "min/max space to a butted P/NCOMP: 0" and NP.3e/PP.3e "space to
# related P/NCOMP edge adjacent to a butting edge: 0": an implant never covers
# COMP of the other type [PV: ncomp.and(pcomp), nplus.and(pcomp)].
rule NP.3d forbidden(ncomp and pcomp)
rule NP.3e forbidden(nplus and pcomp)
rule PP.3d forbidden(pcomp and ncomp)
rule PP.3e forbidden(pplus and ncomp)
# NP.6/PP.6 "overlap with NCOMP (PCOMP) butted to PCOMP (NCOMP): 0.22": the
# butted COMP is at least 0.22 um deep, measured from the other COMP's edges
# to the COMP's own far edges, coincident edges (the butted COMP's shared
# outline) not measured [PV: comp.interacting(nplus).enclosing(pcomp
# .interacting(nplus), 0.22, projection)].
rule NP.6 enclosure(pcomp.interacting(nplus), comp.interacting(nplus), noncoincident) >= 220nm
rule PP.6 enclosure(ncomp.interacting(pplus), comp.interacting(pplus), noncoincident) >= 220nm
# CO.5a/b: a contact on butted COMP is inside its own implant's COMP by 0.1 um;
# a butted COMP is one touching the other type and sharing no area with it
# [PV: ncomp.interacting(pcomp).not_overlapping(pcomp)].
layer ncomp_butted = ncomp.interacting(pcomp).outside(pcomp)
layer pcomp_butted = pcomp.interacting(ncomp).outside(ncomp)
rule CO.5a enclosure(contact.interacting(ncomp_butted), ncomp_butted) >= 100nm
rule CO.5b enclosure(contact.interacting(pcomp_butted), pcomp_butted) >= 100nm
# CO.6a, Vn.3c, Vn.4b "Metal (< 0.34 um) end-of-line overlap: 0.06": a cut on
# metal narrower than 0.34 um needs 0.06 um on both ends of one axis. On a
# narrow wire that is its end of line; at a narrow L-shaped corner it is
# stricter than [PV], which reads only an edge shorter than 0.34 um between
# two edges at least 0.24 um (0.28 um for Vn) long (ledger CO.6a).
rule CO.6a enclosure(contact, metal1, opposite; below: 340nm) >= 60nm
let via_eol = [(V1.3c, V1.4b, via1, metal1, metal2), (V2.3c, V2.4b, via2, metal2, metal3),
               (V3.3c, V3.4b, via3, metal3, metal4), (V4.3c, V4.4b, via4, metal4, metal5),
               (V5.3c, V5.4b, via5, metal5, metaltop)]
for (lo_id, hi_id, v, below, above) in via_eol {
    rule {lo_id} enclosure(v, below, opposite; below: 340nm) >= 60nm
    rule {hi_id} enclosure(v, above, opposite; below: 340nm) >= 60nm
}
# ESD.4a "extension beyond NCOMP: 0.24", except where the NCOMP butts PCOMP
# [PV: esd edges not interacting pcomp]; ESD.6 "extension perpendicular to
# Poly2 gate: 0.45", from the gate's sides on Poly2's edges; ESD.pl "minimum
# gate length of 5V/6V gate NMOS: 0.8", across the gate between its sides on
# Poly2's edges, for gates of Poly2 overlapping Dualgate and touching the ESD
# implant [PV esd.rb].
rule ESD.4a enclosure(ncomp.interacting(esd).edges().not_interacting(pcomp), esd) >= 240nm
rule ESD.6 enclosure((gate.edges() and poly2.edges()).interacting(esd), esd) >= 450nm
rule ESD.pl width(gate.interacting(poly2.overlapping(dualgate).interacting(esd)).edges() and poly2.edges()) >= 800nm
# NAT.4/NAT.5 "minimum channel length for 3.3V (6.0V) native Vt NMOS: 1.8"
# [PV nat.rb: the 3.3 V gates touch neither V5_XTOR nor Dualgate, the 6 V
# gates overlap Dualgate].
rule NAT.4 width((ngate and nat).not_interacting(v5_xtor).not_interacting(dualgate).edges() and poly2.edges()) >= 1800nm
rule NAT.5 width((ngate and nat).overlapping(dualgate).edges() and poly2.edges()) >= 1800nm
# PRES.6/LRES.6 "minimum salicide block overlap of Poly2 resistor in width
# direction: 0.28": the resistor's sides under SAB, out to SAB's edge (its
# heads leave the SAB, so their edges are not held) [PV: pres_poly.enclosed(sab, 0.28)].
rule PRES.6 enclosure(pres_poly.edges().inside_part(sab), sab) >= 280nm
rule LRES.6 enclosure(lres_poly.edges().inside_part(sab), sab) >= 280nm
# PL.6 "90 deg bends on the COMP are not allowed": a turn of Poly2 inside
# COMP. [PV] also flags a Poly2 ending inside COMP (its convex corners), which
# this deck leaves to PL.4's endcap (ledger PL.6).
rule PL.6 bend(poly2, comp)
# MIMTM.8b "maximum single MIM cap area 100 x 100 um2" [PV: with_area above 10000 um2].
rule MIMTM.8b forbidden(fusetop.with_area(> 10000um2))
# DN.3 "each DNWELL shall be directly surrounded by PCOMP guard ring": a
# DNWELL in no hole of a PCOMP ring, or in a ring's hole that also holds
# NCOMP, Nwell or NAT not touching the DNWELL [PV dnwell.rb dn3_l1, dn3_l2].
# [PV] also counts a ring only when its hole meets exactly one DNWELL, which
# no kind counts (ledger DN.3). That the ring is tied to the substrate is LVS's.
layer dn3_ring = pcomp.holes() not pcomp
rule DN.3 forbidden((dnwell not dn3_ring) or dnwell.inside(dn3_ring.covering((nat or ncomp or nwell).not_interacting(dnwell))))

# --- Latch-up [DRM 55 LU, 56 IO] ---
# LU.1-LU.4: the LV column's tap distance from every point of a COMP, by the
# space x (y) from a well edge to the COMP of the other type within 50 um:
# 15 um below 1 um, 30 um below 2 um, 50 um from 2 um. The MV column is 15 um
# whatever the space; LU.3 and LU.4 at MV are DF.14_5V and DF.13_5V above.
let lu_bands = [1um, 2um]
let lu_limits = [15um, 30um, 50um]
rule LU.1 conditional_tie(pcomp_dn_nolvp, ntap_dn, lvpwell_in_dn, pcomp_dn_nolvp; within: 50um, spacing: lu_bands, max_distance: lu_limits)
rule LU.2 conditional_tie(ncomp_lvp, pcomp_lvp, lvpwell_in_dn, pcomp_dn_nolvp; within: 50um, spacing: lu_bands, max_distance: lu_limits)
rule LU.3 conditional_tie(ncomp_psub, ptap, nwell_out_dn, ncomp_psub; within: 50um, spacing: lu_bands, max_distance: lu_limits)
rule LU.4 conditional_tie(pcomp_nw, ntap, nwell_out_dn, ncomp_psub; within: 50um, spacing: lu_bands, max_distance: lu_limits)
rule LU.1_MV missing_tie(pcomp_dn_nolvp_hv, ntap_dn; max_distance: 15um)
rule LU.2_MV missing_tie(ncomp_lvp_hv, pcomp_lvp; max_distance: 15um)
# LU.5: NAT within 50 um of an Nwell is surrounded by a PCOMP substrate ring,
# "No other NCOMP, NWELL in between the NAT and PCOMP guard ring": the ring's
# hole holds no NCOMP or Nwell outside the NAT.
layer lu5_between = ncomp or nwell
rule LU.5 guard_ring(nat, pcomp_psub; max_space: none, min_width: none, pad: none, near: nwell, within: 50um, clear: lu5_between)
# IO.1/IO.3 (a2): COMP on a pad net is surrounded by a guard ring (NCOMP in
# Nwell for NCOMP in the substrate, substrate PCOMP for PCOMP in Nwell) at most
# 15 um away; IO.2/IO.4: the ring is at least 2 um wide ("recommended", so a
# warning). A pad net stands in for Latchup_MK, which marks the same COMP
# (IO.0, a guideline). IO.1/IO.3 (b): within 15 (10) um of that COMP, every
# point of the other COMP type is within 2 (5) um of a tap. (a1), "surrounded
# by a tap without the other COMP in between, except transistors butted to a
# tap over their full width", is not written.
rule IO.1 guard_ring(ncomp_psub, ntap; max_space: 15um, min_width: none, pad: pad, near: none, within: none, clear: none)
rule IO.1b latchup_victim(ncomp_psub, pcomp_in_nw, ntap; within: 15um, max_distance: 2um, pad: pad, bias: none, forward: none)
rule IO.2 warning guard_ring(ncomp_psub, ntap; max_space: none, min_width: 2um, pad: pad, near: none, within: none, clear: none)
rule IO.3 guard_ring(pcomp_nw, pcomp_psub; max_space: 15um, min_width: none, pad: pad, near: none, within: none, clear: none)
rule IO.3b latchup_victim(pcomp_nw, ncomp_psub, ptap; within: 10um, max_distance: 5um, pad: pad, bias: none, forward: none)
rule IO.4 warning guard_ring(pcomp_nw, pcomp_psub; max_space: none, min_width: 2um, pad: pad, near: none, within: none, clear: none)

# --- Rules not written yet ---
# needs: same/diff-net spacing. Net spacing takes a conductor, and the wells
# are not conductors in this deck (no well-tap connection):
#   rule DN.2b space(dnwell; nets: different) >= 5.42um
#   rule LPW.2a_3.3V space(lvpwell; nets: different) >= 1.4um
#   rule LPW.2a_5V space(lvpwell_hv; nets: different) >= 1.7um
#   rule NW.2b_3.3V space(nwell; nets: different) >= 1.4um
#   rule NW.2b_5V space(nwell_hv; nets: different) >= 1.7um
# DF.12 (COMP not under Nplus or Pplus): the schottky marker it exempts is not declared.
#   rule DF.12 forbidden(comp.not_interacting(schottky_diode) not (nplus or pplus))
# Which layer holds which is not confirmed against the manual:
#   rule LPW.5 must_contain(dnwell, lvpwell.inside(res_mk))
#   rule MIMTM.7 must_contain(cap_mk, fusetop)
#   rule NAT.8 must_contain(dualgate, nat_hv)
# Expressible, not written: each is conditional on a band from a well edge
# ([PV] sizes the well by 0.43 um) or on the gate's extension, and needs that
# band as a layer and its own check against the fd_pv unit structures:
#   NP.3a..3c, PP.3a..3c (implant space to the other COMP, 0.16 / 0.08 um),
#   NP.4a/4b, PP.4a/4b (space to the other channel's gate at a butting edge),
#   NP.5b..5dii, PP.5b..5dii (implant extension beyond COMP), NP.11/12, PP.11/12.
# CO.6b, Vn.3d, Vn.4c ("if the metal overlaps the cut by < 0.04 um on one side,
#   the adjacent edges overlap by 0.06 um"): a condition on one side setting
#   the limit of its neighbours, which no enclosure kind reads.
# HRES.9: [PV] also flags SAB edges inside the resistor and SAB holes over it,
#   and its unit structures fail a resistor the SAB encloses by 0.28 um on
#   every side; the manual's "in width direction" does not say why.
# PL.2_6V gate length >= 700nm (6V n), 550nm (6V p): no 6V marker is declared
#   (PL.2 3.3V/5V are coded above).
# --- Left out ---
# Not expressible, and not one of the kinds above:
#   SB.14a/14b (square-metric space 0.56um), SB.15a/15b, SB.16, DV.9, NAT.6, NAT.9,
#   MIMTM.11 (total MIM area on one shared bottom plate: total_area is per chip),
#   MT30.* (30 kA top metal only), ANT.14/ANT.15 (MIM-area antenna: the victim
#   is FuseTop, which no connect row joins to the MetalTop above it), DE.*, the LDMOS (MDN/MDP), OTP, eFuse,
#   SRAM and scribe-line sections.
# Devices not recognised: every diode (np/pn/nwp/dnwpw/dnwps/sc_diode), the
#   nwell and pwell resistors, the vertical BJTs and the inversion-mode MOS
#   capacitors take a terminal on a well or the substrate, which is not a net
#   here; MIM (cap_mim_1p0fF/1p5fF/2p0fF) is a process option the layout
#   does not show; LDMOS source and drain are asymmetric layers.
# well_bias needs a bulk terminal, which needs wells as nets (as above).
# No number in the open manual: absolute maximum device voltages (the
#   voltage rows use the nominal 3.3 V and 6 V), electromigration Blech
#   length and activation energy (electromigration rows are left out; the
#   instantaneous limits are in the EM.* rows).
